1.Difference between smoke and sanity testing?

Smoke Testing:
Smoke testing checks whether the basic and critical functionalities of the application work after a new build, to decide if the build is stable for further testing.

Sanity Testing:
Sanity testing verifies a specific bug fix or change to ensure it works correctly before continuing with detailed testing.

2. Difference between black box and white box testing?

Black Box Testing:
Black box testing checks the functionality of the application without knowing the internal code, focusing only on inputs and expected outputs.

White Box Testing:
White box testing checks the internal code, logic, and structure of the application to ensure all paths and conditions work correctly.

3. Different Levels of Testing

Different Levels of Testing:
 Unit Testing: Tests individual units or components of the application to ensure they work correctly.
 Integration Testing: Checks whether different modules work together properly.
 System Testing: Tests the complete application as a whole against requirements.
 User Acceptance Testing (UAT): Validates the application with end users to ensure it meets business needs.
